Amoxicillin is a broad-spectrum antibiotic. It is commonly used to treat respiratory and urinary tract infections. The drug penetrates the placenta and is excreted in breast milk. Caution is advised for pregnant or lactating women; use only under medical supervision.

Classify this article for teratogenicity warnings:

{{Infobox drug
| pregnancy_AU = D
| pregnancy_US = X
}}
Methotrexate is a chemotherapy agent and immune system suppressant. It is used to treat certain types of cancer, rheumatoid arthritis, and psoriasis. Common side effects include nausea, fatigue, and increased risk of infection.
